Host Discovery with ARP
When our device is connected on the local network and perform -sn scanning using nmap for that local network, nmap will using 
ARP protocol as a priority option, because in the case of the same local network, using ARP is more reliable than using ICMP.
Our attack machine will send a ARP Broadcast Requests(Layer 2) to all devices that is available within a range of the network,
and waiting for ARP reply to identify target status.


